    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Fail-closed honesty (V34)",
      "items": [
        "Only a VALIDATED scheme backs marking (G-2) — anything else returns an honest SCHEME_NOT_VALIDATED row at zero LLM cost",
        "Refusals are honest rows: SCHEME_NOT_VALIDATED (pre-LLM gate), UNPARSEABLE_OUTPUT, TRUNCATED_OUTPUT — the completion budget scales with the point's marks and truncated raw output is persisted",
        "A FLAGGED scheme never backs marking, from SUGGESTED or VALIDATED",
        "SMART_MARKED stays provisional until the κ gate passes; the threshold is recorded per evaluation row",
        "First real κ: agent calibration (n=25, any-credit convention pinned in core e7a55fe), then the operator's genuine human round — κ=1.0 (n=113, threshold 0.60) PASSED; that gate row supersedes the agent round's unvouchable one"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Release & evidence rules",
      "items": [
        "Human marks are authoritative and always visible; AI marks reach learners only after κ ≥ 0.60 (default, per-row)",
        "The first authoritative mark fires learning evidence exactly once (DECISION_016) — overrides revise marks, never re-fire evidence",
        "Independent learners are never blocked by teacher marking (ADR-027 D2): self-mark or κ-gated Smart Mark, SMART_MARKED is a correct terminal state",
        "Answer lifecycle: PENDING → SMART_MARKED (provisional) → HUMAN_MARKED (authoritative); SELF_MARKED / OVERRIDDEN on the same lifecycle"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Scope honesty (ADR-027)",
      "items": [
        "The queue currently reads globally in documented pilot-scope mode (the ADR-015 shortcut)",
        "The classroom lane must ship enrollment-scoped reads in the same milestone — a global read behind a live authorization model is a defect, not a cleanup item",
        "κ calibration samples originate only where a human marker holds authorization (D3); no new teacher accounts until then"
      ]
    }
  ]
